*Solution Steps Walkthrough:*

1. Choose a normalized trial wavefunction $psi_((alpha))$ containing one or more variational parameters $alpha$.

2. Compute the expectation value of the Hamiltonian $E(alpha) = chevron.l psi_((alpha)) bar.v H bar.v psi_((alpha)) chevron.r$.

3. Minimize the energy expectation value with respect to the variational parameter by solving $dif / (dif alpha) E(alpha) = 0$.

4. The minimum value $E(alpha_(min))$ provides an upper bound for the ground state energy of the system: $E_(g s) <= E(alpha_(min))$.
